    ":question/math-academy-id": "e-15609",
    ":question/problem": "What is the amplitude of the function $f(x) = -2\\sin\\left(x-\\dfrac\\pi 3\\right) + 1?$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Given a function in the form $f(x)= A\\sin(Bx +C) + D,$ the amplitude is $|A|.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $A=-2.$ Therefore, the amplitude is $|A|=2.$"
