      ":question/id": "86dec134-c288-5f12-9971-6b0570d7076d",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-117576",
      ":question/problem": "What is the amplitude of the function $f(x)=\\frac{3-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{5}?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that we can rewrite the function as follows:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{3-9\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{5}=-\\frac{9}{5}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nNow, given a function in the form $f(x)=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the amplitude is $|A|.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $A=-\\frac{9}{5}.$ Therefore, the amplitude is $|A|=|-\\frac{9}{5}|=\\frac{9}{5}.$"
    },
