      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-53428",
      ":question/problem": "What is the amplitude of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{3})?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Given a function in the form $f(x)=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the amplitude is $|A|.$ \n\nSince $A=1,$ we have that the amplitude is $|A|=|1|=1.$"
